// "Convert [permanent]" [CR#701.28a]: turn it so that its other face is up,
// under the transform rules. Converting is transforming written with another
// verb: a "transforms into" ability triggers if the object either transforms
// or converts [CR#701.27e], and "can't transform" forbids converting too
// [CR#701.28f]. So the word is this declaration's and the event is
// Transform's: the body is the transform action, with its deed, and convert
// names no deed of its own (`deed: None`), or converting would enact twice.
// Lean `convert`, a Template expanding to `transform`.
KeywordAction(
    name: "convert",
    params: [Subject],
    spelling: "convert <Param(0)>",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "convert",
        frame_set: Transitive,
    ),
    deed: None,
    body: transform(Param(0)),
)
